1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:01,180
Okay.

2
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:02,160
Pick up your phone.

3
00:00:02,180 --> 00:00:03,420
Remember this little box?

4
00:00:03,440 --> 00:00:05,340
Allow this app to track your activity?

5
00:00:05,531 --> 00:00:07,871
You probably tapped, Ask App Not to Track,

6
00:00:07,891 --> 00:00:09,051
without even thinking.

7
00:00:09,177 --> 00:00:11,117
Millions of people did the same thing.

8
00:00:11,137 --> 00:00:12,917
And Meta, the company behind Facebook,

9
00:00:12,937 --> 00:00:14,857
Instagram and WhatsApp, says that one tap

10
00:00:14,877 --> 00:00:16,917
would cost it around ten billion dollars.

11
00:00:17,119 --> 00:00:18,139
I'm Vio.

12
00:00:18,219 --> 00:00:19,659
This is the story of how one button

13
00:00:19,679 --> 00:00:21,519
started a war between two of the richest

14
00:00:21,539 --> 00:00:22,959
companies on Earth.

15
00:00:23,052 --> 00:00:24,932
And how Mark Zuckerberg is now trying to

16
00:00:24,952 --> 00:00:27,012
win it with an AI that shops for you.

17
00:00:27,333 --> 00:00:29,493
First, you need to understand one thing.

18
00:00:29,513 --> 00:00:30,633
Meta owns the apps.

19
00:00:30,653 --> 00:00:31,973
But it doesn't own the phones.

20
00:00:32,174 --> 00:00:34,174
Almost every Instagram scroll and every

21
00:00:34,194 --> 00:00:36,094
WhatsApp message happens on a phone made

22
00:00:36,114 --> 00:00:38,334
by Apple, or running Google's software.

23
00:00:38,391 --> 00:00:40,491
So Meta is like a shop that pays rent in

24
00:00:40,511 --> 00:00:41,851
somebody else's building.

25
00:00:41,907 --> 00:00:44,447
It's a huge, very rich shop.

26
00:00:44,467 --> 00:00:46,267
But the landlord still makes the rules.

27
00:00:46,445 --> 00:00:48,205
And for years, Apple had been telling

28
00:00:48,225 --> 00:00:50,425
everyone that it was the privacy company.

29
00:00:50,625 --> 00:00:52,105
It even put up a giant billboard in Las

30
00:00:52,125 --> 00:00:54,705
Vegas saying, what happens on your iPhone,

31
00:00:54,725 --> 00:00:55,945
stays on your iPhone.

32
00:00:56,337 --> 00:00:58,257
And Meta's business runs on ads.

33
00:00:58,697 --> 00:00:59,717
Really good ads.

34
00:00:59,877 --> 00:01:01,457
Ads that seem to know you.

35
00:01:01,557 --> 00:01:02,897
Say you look at a pair of sneakers in a

36
00:01:02,917 --> 00:01:03,897
shopping app.

37
00:01:04,037 --> 00:01:05,737
Ten minutes later, those exact sneakers

38
00:01:05,757 --> 00:01:07,217
show up on Instagram.

39
00:01:07,417 --> 00:01:08,797
That works because your iPhone had a

40
00:01:08,817 --> 00:01:10,017
hidden ID number.

41
00:01:10,277 --> 00:01:11,497
Apps could use it to follow you from one

42
00:01:11,517 --> 00:01:13,697
app to another, and tell Meta what you did.

43
00:01:13,735 --> 00:01:15,475
It had a very boring name.

44
00:01:15,595 --> 00:01:16,575
The I D F A.

45
00:01:16,595 --> 00:01:18,135
The identifier for advertisers.

46
00:01:18,535 --> 00:01:19,935
But it was worth a fortune.

47
00:01:20,088 --> 00:01:21,408
Think of it as a little spy,

48
00:01:21,428 --> 00:01:23,088
quietly following you everywhere you go on

49
00:01:23,108 --> 00:01:23,908
your phone.

50
00:01:23,948 --> 00:01:25,308
And advertisers paid a lot for what that

51
00:01:25,328 --> 00:01:26,428
spy saw.

52
00:01:26,451 --> 00:01:27,591
And here's the thing.

53
00:01:27,611 --> 00:01:30,191
Most people had no idea the spy was there.

54
00:01:30,522 --> 00:01:32,562
Then, in April 2021,

55
00:01:32,942 --> 00:01:35,582
Apple released iOS fourteen point five.

56
00:01:35,651 --> 00:01:37,891
Now every app had to ask first.

57
00:01:38,011 --> 00:01:39,431
Do you want this app to track you,

58
00:01:39,451 --> 00:01:40,511
yes or no?

59
00:01:40,540 --> 00:01:41,880
Meta saw it coming.

60
00:01:42,140 --> 00:01:43,840
Months earlier, it bought full-page ads in

61
00:01:43,860 --> 00:01:45,640
big American newspapers, saying,

62
00:01:45,660 --> 00:01:46,760
we're standing up to Apple for small

63
00:01:46,780 --> 00:01:48,160
businesses everywhere.

64
00:01:48,259 --> 00:01:49,899
Apple's answer was simple.

65
00:01:50,119 --> 00:01:52,759
It said this was about standing up for its users.

66
00:01:52,917 --> 00:01:54,677
Imagine your landlord putting a big sign

67
00:01:54,697 --> 00:01:57,097
on your shop door, asking every customer,

68
00:01:57,157 --> 00:01:59,077
do you want this shop to watch what you do?

69
00:01:59,217 --> 00:02:00,997
Most people are going to say no.

70
00:02:01,060 --> 00:02:02,700
And the users chose.

71
00:02:02,720 --> 00:02:04,420
In the first weeks, one analytics company

72
00:02:04,440 --> 00:02:06,480
estimated that only around four to six

73
00:02:06,500 --> 00:02:09,320
percent of iPhone users in the US said yes.

74
00:02:09,770 --> 00:02:11,590
Meta's ads got less precise.

75
00:02:12,110 --> 00:02:13,630
Advertisers couldn't see as clearly what

76
00:02:13,650 --> 00:02:15,790
was working, so they spent less.

77
00:02:15,935 --> 00:02:18,075
In February 2022, Meta told its investors

78
00:02:18,095 --> 00:02:19,935
the Apple change would cost it about ten

79
00:02:19,955 --> 00:02:21,435
billion dollars that year.

80
00:02:21,455 --> 00:02:23,035
Its own finance chief called that number a

81
00:02:23,055 --> 00:02:24,055
best guess.

82
00:02:24,081 --> 00:02:25,941
The next day, Meta's stock fell about

83
00:02:25,961 --> 00:02:27,381
twenty six percent.

84
00:02:27,452 --> 00:02:28,892
Roughly two hundred and thirty billion

85
00:02:28,912 --> 00:02:31,572
dollars in value disappeared in a single day.

86
00:02:31,592 --> 00:02:33,452
At the time, the biggest one-day drop for

87
00:02:33,472 --> 00:02:35,470
any American company in history.

88
00:02:35,490 --> 00:02:36,410
One button.

89
00:02:36,430 --> 00:02:37,910
Ten billion dollars a year.

90
00:02:37,970 --> 00:02:39,250
That's about twenty seven million dollars,

91
00:02:39,270 --> 00:02:40,570
every single day.

92
00:02:40,863 --> 00:02:42,563
So Zuckerberg needed a way out of the

93
00:02:42,583 --> 00:02:43,703
landlord's building.

94
00:02:43,857 --> 00:02:45,557
First, he bet on the metaverse.

95
00:02:45,697 --> 00:02:47,497
Then the AI race exploded,

96
00:02:47,537 --> 00:02:48,917
and Meta was suddenly chasing companies

97
00:02:48,937 --> 00:02:50,817
like OpenAI and Google.

98
00:02:50,957 --> 00:02:53,137
Meta built its own AI models and gave many

99
00:02:53,157 --> 00:02:54,617
of them away for free.

100
00:02:54,857 --> 00:02:57,157
But for a while, rivals kept pulling ahead.

101
00:02:57,241 --> 00:02:59,181
So Meta started spending like crazy.

102
00:02:59,421 --> 00:03:01,421
Billions on a new superintelligence team,

103
00:03:01,441 --> 00:03:03,821
and, reportedly, pay packages for top AI

104
00:03:03,841 --> 00:03:05,261
researchers that sounded like football

105
00:03:05,281 --> 00:03:06,501
transfer fees.

106
00:03:07,241 --> 00:03:10,101
And in September 2026, Meta showed what

107
00:03:10,121 --> 00:03:11,601
all that money was for.

108
00:03:11,861 --> 00:03:13,621
An AI agent called Muse.

109
00:03:13,879 --> 00:03:15,119
Muse doesn't just chat.

110
00:03:15,139 --> 00:03:16,179
It does things.

111
00:03:16,199 --> 00:03:17,559
You can ask it to plan a trip,

112
00:03:17,579 --> 00:03:19,479
send an email, or buy you something.

113
00:03:19,555 --> 00:03:21,035
Meta says it can check out from stores

114
00:03:21,055 --> 00:03:23,355
like Walmart, Best Buy and Sephora,

115
00:03:23,375 --> 00:03:25,295
and it lives right inside WhatsApp.

116
00:03:25,465 --> 00:03:27,125
It's free to start, with paid plans at

117
00:03:27,145 --> 00:03:28,945
twenty and a hundred dollars a month.

118
00:03:29,025 --> 00:03:31,465
For now, it's only available in the United States.

119
00:03:31,662 --> 00:03:33,282
Now think about what that means.

120
00:03:33,302 --> 00:03:34,762
If you tell Muse what you want,

121
00:03:34,782 --> 00:03:36,682
there's no need for a spy to follow you around.

122
00:03:36,702 --> 00:03:37,862
You just told it yourself.

123
00:03:38,052 --> 00:03:39,832
And because it all happens inside Meta's

124
00:03:39,852 --> 00:03:41,872
own apps, Apple's little box never even

125
00:03:41,892 --> 00:03:42,807
pops up.

126
00:03:42,827 --> 00:03:44,387
And at its big event,

127
00:03:44,567 --> 00:03:45,847
Zuckerberg even described a possible

128
00:03:45,867 --> 00:03:47,987
future where Muse takes a small cut of the

129
00:03:48,007 --> 00:03:49,347
things it buys for you.

130
00:03:49,487 --> 00:03:50,967
So Meta could earn from the ad,

131
00:03:50,987 --> 00:03:52,087
and from the sale.

132
00:03:52,499 --> 00:03:55,139
Meta is also bringing Muse to its smart glasses.

133
00:03:55,619 --> 00:03:56,319
Picture this.

134
00:03:56,479 --> 00:03:57,819
You see a jacket on the street,

135
00:03:57,839 --> 00:03:59,139
you ask your glasses about it,

136
00:03:59,159 --> 00:04:00,619
and a few seconds later, it's on its way

137
00:04:00,639 --> 00:04:01,379
to you.

138
00:04:01,410 --> 00:04:03,150
That's either the coolest thing ever,

139
00:04:03,170 --> 00:04:04,170
or the creepiest.

140
00:04:04,190 --> 00:04:05,130
Maybe both.

141
00:04:05,219 --> 00:04:07,899
And remember, Muse can make mistakes.

142
00:04:08,199 --> 00:04:10,159
And reportedly, Meta's own terms limit

143
00:04:10,179 --> 00:04:11,699
what it pays back if the agent buys

144
00:04:11,719 --> 00:04:13,139
something you didn't want.

145
00:04:13,228 --> 00:04:14,908
So here's my question.

146
00:04:15,068 --> 00:04:17,188
Would you let Meta's AI spend your money?

147
00:04:17,308 --> 00:04:18,408
Tell me in the comments.

148
00:04:18,619 --> 00:04:19,579
And subscribe.

149
00:04:19,959 --> 00:04:21,619
Next time, there's another tech war you

150
00:04:21,639 --> 00:04:23,099
didn't know was happening.

151
00:04:23,168 --> 00:04:24,628
Apple took away the button.

152
00:04:24,648 --> 00:04:26,708
Now Meta wants to become the button.
